{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>If not:</b> This connects to what precedes it: 'almost had my haters governed me — had I not trusted in HaShem and said to my soul: hope to YHWH, then the uprightness of my words would be proven, for I was reproving and saying: hope to YHWH.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The comment assumes the reconstructed reading לולא האמנתי (had I not trusted) against the Masoretic לולא האמנתי, interpreting the phrase as a conditional completed by verse 14."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:45.902253619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}